course: dictionary
lesson: 2390
title: Curly: from hair to spirals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Curly is a describing word. It tells you about the shape of something. Most of the time it means having curls, like hair that grows in rings or waves. «When they bow, their curly wigs get tangled, and Alice has to run off to hide her laughter.» The wigs are full of curls, so they tangle easily.
explain: Curly can also mean shaped in curves or spirals. «Picture a beach after a storm: among the seaweed lies a black leathery pouch with curly corners.» The corners are not hair. They are twisted into curls, so curly describes their shape.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Ask yourself: is this thing made of hair, or is it bent into curves? The sentence before or after will often tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Curly means having curls, like hair that grows in rings or waves.
fact: Curly also means shaped in curves or spirals, like a curly tail or curly writing.
fact: Curlier is the comparison of one thing, and curliest is the comparison of the most: «Her hair is curlier than mine, but his is the curliest.»
fact: In maths, curly brackets { } are used to group numbers into sets.
fact: «Curly tendrils» are thin twisting stems that wrap round sticks to hold a plant up, like the tendrils of a pea plant.
exercise: «Her curly hair bounced when she ran.» What does curly mean here? | Very wet from the rain | Straight and flat | *Having curls, like hair in rings or waves | Dark brown in colour
exercise: «The pea plant's curly tendrils wrapped round the stick.» What does curly describe in this sentence? | The light from the window | The stick | The plant's roots in the soil | *Tendrils that are twisted in spirals
exercise: Ella says curly brackets are only for hair. Is she right? | No, they are used for weather reports | Yes, they show that someone is very tired | Yes, they are only used for drawings of hair | *No, they group numbers in maths, called sets
test: Which word is the -er form of curly? | curlyest | curliest | curl-ing | *curlier
test: «Eating crusts does not make hair curly.» What is curly describing here? | A shop that sells crusts | Bread that is shaped in spirals | A puppy's tail that is straight | *Hair that has curls
exam: Which sentence uses curly to mean shaped in curves or spirals? | «Her curly hair was tied in a bun.» | «The curly wigs got tangled.» | *«A curly tendril wrapped round the stick.» | «He wore curly wigs to the play.»
